-- 🚨 KNOWN-BAD LEDGER ROW (#1182 / #1265 class, OPEN): this is a DIFFERENT,
-- PRE-EXISTING coverage gap from the #1276/#1386 rows in this file -- NOT
-- something S-alias-supply drained, and NOT something its fix touches. That
-- fix repairs the CHECKED half (impl-obligation existence); this pins the
-- DISPATCH half (which impl's body actually RUNS) still disagreeing with it.
--
-- `Blob` implements BOTH `IA` and `IB`. `A.mth Blob` and `B.mth Blob` are
-- alias-qualified calls that name TWO DIFFERENT interfaces. Correct answer:
-- 1 then 2 (each call dispatches to the impl its own alias names). OBSERVED
-- (slice 2, `cdca5045`, changed which impl the last-write-wins floor picks
-- for the collided name `mth`): 2 then 2 -- NOT value-neutral. Both calls
-- still collapse onto ONE impl on check, run, AND build alike, because
-- `renameAliasedMethods` erases the alias to a bare `mth` before dispatch
-- is decided and ordinary dispatch has no per-alias-occurrence
-- discriminator -- but which impl they collapse onto changed: `admittedIfaceFor
-- "mth"` now answers from the last-write-wins `registerMethodIfaceParamsMethods`
-- table, which resolves to `IB` (declared second) for both calls. So the OLD
-- pinned behavior (1,1) had `A.mth Blob` correct and `B.mth Blob` wrong; the
-- NEW behavior (2,2) has `B.mth Blob` correct and `A.mth Blob` now wrong --
-- still one-of-two wrong, but a different one.
--
-- Witness from F-fix-alias-collision's report (Note N1), confirmed
-- reproducing identically at both the pre-sprint merge-base `9824e65b` and
-- the sprint head -- neither this sprint's fix nor the alias-collision fix
-- caused the ORIGINAL (1,1) misbehavior. THIS ROW IS EXPECTED TO STAY GREEN
-- (i.e. keep reproducing A WRONG value) until #1182/#1265 land; a value
-- change here is the signal to re-pin it, not a regression in this gate.
import ifa.{IA}
import ifb.{IB}
import ifa as A
import ifb as B

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl IA Blob where
  mth b = 1

export impl IB Blob where
  mth b = 2

main =
  let _ = println (A.mth Blob)
  println (B.mth Blob)
